<title>MEXICO: Mexican financial markets closed for May Day.</title>
<headline>Mexican financial markets closed for May Day.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican financial markets will be closed on Thursday in observance of May Day.</p>
<p>The Mexican stock, money and currency markets will not trade, and banks and government offices will be closed.</p>
<p>President Ernesto Zedillo is scheduled to address the Confederation of Mexican Workers (CTM), a six-million-strong pro-government labor organization, while indepedent unions have scheduled a march on Mexico City's central plaza.</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9507))</p>
